Boundary notes:
  cert-manager = the Kubernetes certificate-issuance controller (Certificate, Issuer,
  ClusterIssuer, CertificateRequest, Order, Challenge CRDs) and its companion tools
  (trust-manager, CSI driver). It does NOT own the ACME CA itself (lets-encrypt), Vault's PKI
  engine internals (hashicorp-vault-ops), the PKI concept layer (secrets-hygiene), or
  certificate-validity UTC arithmetic (utc-timestamps).
  lets-encrypt owns the ACME CA and out-of-Kubernetes ACME clients. cert-manager points its
  ACME ClusterIssuer at the Let's Encrypt directory URL; that consuming relationship is the
  link between the two skills.

